1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:04,700
One dream, one wish.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,240
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,400
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no!

6
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,837
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

7
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:41,397
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:44,180
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

9
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,477
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you?

10
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:56,420
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,537
Despite all that to run is not an option.

12
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,637
Once they're closed, they
feel the satisfaction.

13
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,337
If you are going on your way?

16
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day?

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:19,257
Then make sure your only
thought you have is Yes, I can!

18
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,057
As you're on your way?

19
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,337
Marked maps will be made.

20
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

21
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

22
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

23
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,977
In view shining brightly.

24
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,860
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you?

25
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,117
Dream living, that's the way.

26
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,197
Make like a hurricane.

27
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

28
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:51,177
One dream, one wish.

29
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

30
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:56,020
Go for the knockout.

31
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:03,240
You doubted the loyalty of my crew.

32
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,900
I won't forget it.

33
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,677
At times like these, we
have to focus on the battle!

34
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:12,517
and trust each other completely?

35
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,953
or we'll die out there.

36
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:23,698
I get why he was mad, but
he didn't have to ditch us.

37
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:25,200
Hope he comes back.

38
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,840
Frickin' Shinobu!

39
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,897
She really screwed this one up for us!

40
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:33,017
You can't really blame her
for acting that way, though.

41
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:35,276
Kaido came in, took over her country,

42
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:38,360
trashed it, and screwed up
her life in the process.

43
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:42,405
She's been waiting 20 long years
for this plan to come together.

44
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,020
I getcha.

45
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,137
But even if Law's crew did rent us
out, I couldn't blame them either.

46
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,050
Yeah?

47
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:50,197
Because that's what you would do?

48
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,110
Oh, please.

49
00:02:51,193 --> 00:02:52,728
You'd squeal in one minute.

50
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:58,740
Uh, if I was being tortured,
more like three seconds.

51
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:01,720
That's too short even
for me! Piss off! Huh?

52
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,640
I don't need help from lower-class scum!

53
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,860
What the heck?

54
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,440
Since when does anyone get
angry in Ebisu town anyway?

55
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,880
I see.

56
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,660
This must be that hag
monster's curse! God!

57
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,887
They must be the new fellas.

58
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:19,817
They arrived from the capital.

59
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,194
I heard they were kicked out yesterday.

60
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,820
What are you looking at?

61
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:26,039
You little squirts better get lost.

62
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,760
They were forced out?

63
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,150
Yes.

64
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,917
Only those who are loyal to the Shogun and

65
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,647
can make profits are
permitted to live there.

66
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,340
But from what I heard?

67
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,877
Those men were up to some bad business.

68
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,607
and earned their banishment.

69
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,470
See him?

70
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,388
That's Bongo the underling.

71
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,780
That one was into some
real naughty business.

72
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:57,100
He went around setting fires at night, but
paid off officials to avoid punishment.

73
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:01,940
An arsonist?

74
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,297
He paid bribes just to torment people?

75
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,097
It was more than just a hobby.

76
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:08,298
He was in cahoots with someone else,

77
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:11,837
namely a lumber dealer who sold supplies?

78
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,626
for rebuilding burned houses.

79
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:15,260
That's bongo.

80
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:19,170
Huh?

81
00:04:19,253 --> 00:04:21,040
That's not all, I'm afraid.

82
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:25,840
A third man, a priest and undertaker,
exploited the fire victims.

83
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,457
In their time of mourning, he
gouged them on funeral costs.

84
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,720
That's bingo.

85
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,480
That's awful.

86
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,620
They were working together? Yes.

87
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,900
Bingo Bongo and Bungo are our bad bunch.

88
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,700
A band of bamboozlers.

89
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:44,670
Scumbags.

90
00:04:44,753 --> 00:04:45,583
Who does that?

91
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:49,697
Alas, because they paid off the
officials, they weren't arrested.

92
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:53,839
They got away with everything without
so much as a slap on the wrist.

93
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:57,128
On the outside, they
looked like decent men,

94
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:00,064
but on the inside, they
were rotten to the core.

95
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,379
Here's the kicker.

96
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:06,560
All three of them were head over heels
in love with the beautiful Gomorrah Saki.

97
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:10,400
She's the Oiran who met an
untimely death just yesterday.

98
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,577
Apparently, they all went
bankrupt trying to woo her,

99
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,697
throwing all the money
they owned at her feet.

100
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,597
So I suppose they got their
just desserts in the end.

101
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:20,562
Thank the gods.

102
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,297
At least the story ends well.

103
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:23,210
I don't know.

104
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,257
Those rumors seem really specific.

105
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:27,693
But I'm sure they must hold some weight.

106
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:32,620
And the way you tell it, I bet that
Oiran tricked them on purpose. Nice.

107
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,282
I can't help but wonder
what she was really like.

108
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,597
Wait, I know them! Hmm?

109
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,100
I saw them before!

110
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,500
They threw a fit!

111
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:47,937
They were making a big scene
at the Oideron's procession!

112
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:52,577
Yasuie, bless his soul, was helping them
pick out a house and showing them around.

113
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:55,719
Not that those ungrateful
miscreants appreciated it.

114
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,217
Wow, seriously?

115
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,340
What a guy!

116
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:00,780
He really is nice to everyone, huh?

117
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:05,820
I bet you recruited a slew of
new people, so not always lost!

118
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:14,400
Would you please pass on a
message to my pal, Kinamon?

119
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:20,487
Tell him that once the fight starts,
he'll have us at his side, no matter what.

120
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,040
He is your pal, is he?

121
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:30,788
It's been a pleasure
seeing the both of you.

122
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,920
Now, if you'll excuse
me, we've got lots to do.

123
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:35,415
Hey, don't leave yet.

124
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,052
There's no time to lose.

125
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:39,597
Plenty of folks are likely
to die in the next week.

126
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,510
Let's go!

127
00:06:40,593 --> 00:06:43,017
We have our work cut out
for us and then some.

128
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,806
Alrighty, I'll see you later.

129
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,480
Looking sharp, handsome!

130
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,057
You two beautiful...

131
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,120
Good afternoon, young lady.

132
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,160
You three have a wonderful
day now. Take care!

133
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:11,020
Well, that was weird. What's his deal?

134
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:13,777
He was running his mouth
like you were good friends,

135
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:16,077
but I couldn't figure out
how you were connected.

136
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,640
I couldn't tell either.

137
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,715
Yes, I thought he was rather charming.

138
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,597
Are the three of you close?

139
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,510
Who is he?

140
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:28,380
The truth is...

141
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,260
We haven't a clue.

142
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:35,084
Wait, you don't know who he is?

143
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,757
Why'd you talk to him the
whole time without asking?

144
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,600
He just drolled on and on.

145
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,957
I couldn't get word in.

146
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:43,277
How do you forget someone
like that, though?

147
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:47,140
The fact that he spoke to us
with such familiarity puzzled me.

148
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:50,920
Besides that, what if he
indeed was a man of importance?

149
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,040
Alas, I'd look a fool!

150
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,499
Was he a childhood friend of yours?

151
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,040
Or perhaps a mentor?

152
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,439
He seemed so comfortable
and happy in your presence.

153
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,660
Just tell me already!

154
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:08,399
How would we know?

155
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:11,100
I've had enough.

156
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,060
Kill him!

157
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,180
Make him pay!

158
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,520
Hang on tight, okay?

159
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,280
I believe I know what
you mean by Haki now.

160
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:37,780
It's called Riyuo in the land of Wano.

161
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:40,060
Riyuo, huh?

162
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,160
The term means flow.

163
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:51,117
When you're using Haki, you let it
run through your body, don't you?

164
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,420
You must feel it first.

165
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,430
Right!

166
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,660
I just gotta let it flow!

167
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,660
You need to pull back!

168
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,700
I touched him!

169
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:26,780
Messed it up!

170
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:30,280
You're over-stressing yourself.

171
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:35,320
Allow the Haki to move to your fist
from the parts that don't use it.

172
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,740
Your time's up, Straw Hat!

173
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,420
See ya clear!

174
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,600
Still off!

175
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,980
It doesn't work!

176
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,440
What's the trick?

177
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:01,220
Nope! No! Dammit!

178
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:02,940
How do you do it?

179
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,320
I'm getting sick of this!

180
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:10,720
My Haki won't flow the right way!

181
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,000
He just keeps on taking them down.

182
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,359
Can't kill stupid.

183
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:30,210
Damn!

184
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:32,960
Focus your Haki.

185
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:35,081
It won't flow into an angry fist.

186
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:39,620
Who's gonna step up next?

187
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,300
Let's go now!

188
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,780
How do you do, Pops?

189
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,457
How are those old stomach
cramps treating you?

190
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,757
Oh, hello, Yasuie.

191
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:53,397
It's not a lot, but I'm leaving
some millet and water for you.

192
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,040
So make sure to eat up.

193
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:59,060
You're a helpful fellow,
Yasuie. Thank you.

194
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:02,180
Oh, why, it was nothing, nothing at all.

195
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,657
But I'm delighted to help out.

196
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:04,570
Really.

197
00:11:04,653 --> 00:11:05,483
Here.

198
00:11:05,566 --> 00:11:07,437
I'll even throw in another bag for you.

199
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:09,340
See you, pups. Daddy.

200
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,030
Yoo-hoo.

201
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:15,017
Do you have enough medicine,
seaweed shop, sweetie?

202
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,100
I'm afraid not.

203
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,797
But truth be told, seeing
you always cheers me up.

204
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:19,710
Ah!

205
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,645
You talk to everyone that way?

206
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,760
Oh, hey, mister.

207
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:26,240
How's the knee holding up? Yes, Sue.

208
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,420
You want to play?

209
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:29,280
Hey, you Huang.

210
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,187
Is your mama feeling better?

211
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,640
Oh, Saki, how's the baby doing?

212
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,350
Oh!

213
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,220
Over here!

214
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,740
Don't forget to say hi to us, too.

215
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:42,841
Here, everybody.

216
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:45,020
It's not much, but take these.

217
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,475
Thank you, as always.

218
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,760
Wow, he's so generous.

219
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,640
Is he rich? Nice guy.

220
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,901
Spreading his wealth around town.

221
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,460
Quite the contrary.

222
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:58,797
The poor man works himself to
the bone and gets paid peanuts.

223
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:04,420
He has a daughter, a girl named Dock, but
she was sold into a job at the capital.

224
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:08,040
She sends most of her
earnings back here to Yasuie.

225
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,380
We don't say.

226
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:15,720
Dock, that's me!

227
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,360
Oh, it's her.

228
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,560
Since so much of his
money is sent from Dock,

229
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:24,526
he says it isn't right
to keep it for himself.

230
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:28,220
So he goes around and spreads
it to those less fortunate.

231
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:32,400
A blessing for those
of us too weak to work.

232
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:39,537
He may come across as foolish, but
he's a beloved member of our community?

233
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:42,060
who supported us for so long.

234
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,120
He's our saint.

235
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:50,360
I miss you, Daddy.

236
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:55,490
Daddy!

237
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:03,760
We're done for today. Go to sleep!

238
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:06,780
It's not fair.

239
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:09,620
I've got plenty of fight left.

240
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,960
Why do we gotta wait till tomorrow?

241
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,560
I'm hungry.

242
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,920
Aren't you guys going to at least feed us?

243
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,220
Stop yapping like a dog.

244
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:30,140
Shut up and sleep.

245
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:33,380
I'm going to turn into
a mummy by tomorrow.

246
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:37,960
May I ask you something, Mr. Straw Hat?

247
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,080
Go ahead.

248
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,560
Why are you so eager to fight Kaido?

249
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,160
I heard you lost to him in Kuri.

250
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,340
I can't talk yet.

251
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,600
There, that'll work.

252
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,060
Now I'll say it.

253
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,690
Hmm?

254
00:14:07,773 --> 00:14:09,360
You know the Four Emperors?

255
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:10,897
I don't.

256
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:14,097
They're called that because they're
the most powerful pirates out there,

257
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:15,474
supposedly unbeatable.

258
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,780
Well, one of those guys is Kaido.

259
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,737
I'm going to be king of the pirates,

260
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:25,360
so that means I've got to
take them all down to do it.

261
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:27,600
The pirate king?

262
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,400
You want to become a gold roger?

263
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:34,402
Wait, are you saying you
know about him, old man?

264
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:38,300
Yes, he visited the land of
Wano quite some time ago.

265
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,170
Huh.

266
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,774
That lines up with what Keenumont said.

267
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:44,470
Huh?

268
00:14:44,553 --> 00:14:45,383
What did you say?

269
00:14:45,466 --> 00:14:47,257
Are you telling me you know him?

270
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:48,420
Is my hearing off?

271
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:58,240
What is that crap?

272
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:07,620
It can't be! Rizal?

273
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,180
Greetings, Straw Hat.

274
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,600
What the hell?

275
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,100
I don't know.

276
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:20,060
I don't think this is
the real Raizo. It is.

277
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:26,320
Why are you inside that guy?

278
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:29,060
You're still alive, Raizo? How?

279
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:33,020
I shall explain all to you, Sir Hyogoro.

280
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,340
That's him!

281
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,836
It's Uchimichu Koza!

282
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,740
You're cornered now!

283
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,760
Grab him!

284
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:52,500
I can't believe it's really you.

285
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:53,640
It is indeed.

286
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:57,700
And I assure you, I am as surprised
by our meeting as you are.

287
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,080
Oh. Unbelievable.

288
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,680
So tell me,

289
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:06,977
does this mean that your
desperate plan was successful

290
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:09,937
and you really arrived here
for 20 years in the past?

291
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:11,040
Yes, indeed.

292
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,240
Thanks to Lady Toki's sorcery. Hmm.

293
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:17,279
That's incredible.

294
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:20,600
What I don't get is why
you're here, caribou.

295
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:21,760
Go away!

296
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,820
Hey, don't be like that, Straw Hat.

297
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,320
We're pals, aren't we?

298
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:28,020
What gives here, Rhizo?

299
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,717
I thought you only came
here to break me out.

300
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,200
Why are you helping this Garp? Aw.

301
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:35,397
No need to be such a Moon.

302
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:38,520
I might come in handy after all.

303
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,760
I'm your underling.

304
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:42,354
Give me orders, chief.

305
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:48,260
Well, in exchange for just one thing,

306
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:51,707
may I have a ride home
on your ship with you?

307
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,620
Tough luck, pal.

308
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,055
You're stranded here.

309
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,177
But I've realized the error of my ways.

310
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,090
Don't you see?

311
00:16:58,173 --> 00:16:59,548
I'm a changed man, I swear!

312
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,700
Please, sir!

313
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:08,360
Okay, it's a deal, but
only because you changed.

314
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,440
Wow, really?

315
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,660
Thank you!

316
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,960
Is this some kind of trap?

317
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,300
That was way too easy.

318
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,597
Sir Luffy Taro, the groveling fellow
has quite a remarkable skill set.

319
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,920
He shall be of great service to us.

320
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:35,717
For so long, I thought my fate
was sealed, but I didn't give up,

321
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:41,580
I kept clinging on to this
wretched life, I'm so glad!

322
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:45,530
Huh?

323
00:17:45,613 --> 00:17:47,140
Are you all right, sir?

324
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:55,957
How close I came to letting
myself die in this prison,

325
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:59,160
I had accepted death!

326
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:07,920
If this had happened a moment too late, I
might have died, never knowing the truth?

327
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:13,840
So the Akazaya Samurai
are still alive, are they?

328
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:15,500
And that isn't all?

329
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,080
Odin's son Kozuki Momonosuke too?

330
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:21,777
It's more than some tall tale.

331
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:24,960
The rebel's flame still burns bright.

332
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,880
Rise off! And Mr. Straw Hat!

333
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:43,269
I may be old, but for my country's sake,
I will always have fight left in me.

334
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,740
May I join you?

335
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,001
There must be something I can do.

336
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,477
It would be an honor to have you.

337
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:51,720
Sir Luffy,

338
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:56,457
this man kneeling before you was once the
greatest Yakuza boss in the land of Lardo!

339
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:57,370
Yeah?

340
00:18:57,453 --> 00:19:00,400
So you were a big deal
back in the day, old man?

341
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:02,677
You mentioned that you've been gathering

342
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,525
supporters for the cause
in the Flower Capital.

343
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:06,590
Is that right?

344
00:19:06,673 --> 00:19:07,503
Indeed!

345
00:19:07,586 --> 00:19:11,580
Then it really must be fate that
brought you here to Udon, hmm?

346
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:16,217
Located in this labor camp, there
are four other excavation sites?

347
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:18,000
just as vast as this one.

348
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:22,960
Not to mention tens of thousands
of prisoners exactly like us.

349
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:27,477
However, the inmates here were
locked up for petty theft or assault.

350
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:31,297
Nearly every single one of
them are guilty of rebellion.

351
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,737
Against Shogun orgy?

352
00:19:33,820 --> 00:19:35,260
Of course!

353
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:37,520
Why did this not occur to me?

354
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:41,577
The rage of this country is
ready to burst from these gates.

355
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:44,217
The Yakuza leaders who once supported Wano

356
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:46,597
from the shadows are
all held at this prison.

357
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:49,040
I will converse with them.

358
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:52,260
I'm certain that they'll
join the cause for Kozuki.

359
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:55,540
Raizo, see that cell there?

360
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:57,040
Yes, I am aware.

361
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:00,000
I have exchanged words with Kawamatsu.

362
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:03,120
He is the first one that I shall set free.

363
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,040
Perfect, then.

364
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:08,640
All I gotta do is rip this place apart.

365
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:12,324
Then we'll get a whole
crap load of new friends!

366
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:14,640
Sir Luffy, are you mad?

367
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,360
Lower your voice! Right!

368
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,600
Sounds like a plan to me!

369
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,440
Now, give me some drugs!

370
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,597
This is it.

371
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,440
I'm gonna die.

372
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:32,120
I'm hungry, I'm tired, and
there's no horse here to call.

373
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,240
Farewell, Okiku.

374
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:39,900
Our sharkodile is exhausted too, but I'm
happy to say we have already entered Udon.

375
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:45,220
I'm coming for you, my sweet, sweet love.

376
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,740
This might get messy.

377
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,540
It's so good!

378
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,280
I want more!

379
00:20:58,440 --> 00:21:01,260
Wait for me, dear suit.

380
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:07,480
Breaking news!

381
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,900
He's locked up!

382
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:13,700
Ushimitsu Koza, the elusive thief
terrorizing the flower capital, was caught!

383
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:14,920
Read about it!

384
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:16,380
Take a flyer!

385
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:20,540
Lord Orochi, apologies for the intrusion.

386
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:23,055
If I could have a moment of your time.

387
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:26,014
It's concerning that troublesome thief.

388
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,680
We have apprehended him.

389
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:30,740
Silence, you fool!

390
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,517
I am in mourning for the love of my life!

391
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:37,600
You will never understand the pain
of losing such a beautiful woman!

392
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,940
You do have my sympathy, Shogun.

393
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:44,219
I recognize you're experiencing
grief, but with all due respect, sir.

394
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:47,277
Kiyoshiro had to take appropriate actions.

395
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:51,077
If we allowed her transgressions
to pass, you would have lost face.

396
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:55,101
This situation would have undermined
your authority and reputation.

397
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:18,460
Lord Orochi, I don't care about
some miserable little robber.

398
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,137
That's trivial to me.

399
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:23,637
There is no woman alive
who could ever compete

400
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:26,497
with her immense beauty
and I was robbed of her.

401
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:29,051
Can't you see I want to be left to myself?

402
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:32,997
Despite your sorrow, it's nice you
have emerged from your quarters.

403
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,760
But I must strongly
insist you listen to me.

404
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:37,493
The matter is pressing.

405
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:41,284
Ushimitsu Koza was not
your typical petty thief.

406
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:47,597
On the surface, he's a crook with a hero
complex, bent on helping the lower class.

407
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,640
A menace to the rich!

408
00:22:49,820 --> 00:22:53,237
He's run amok on the flower
capital for quite some time now,

409
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:55,380
but something greater is at play.

410
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:58,140
As previously mentioned,

411
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:02,297
he's currently being held at the
prisoner's quarters in Rasetsu Town.

412
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:05,820
But his identity is the interesting part.

413
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:07,490
What?

414
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,780
It can't be!

415
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:25,160
How is the bastard still alive?

416
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:32,480
After all this time Is this a joke?

417
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:35,380
Right under my nose, no less

418
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:37,600
Course me clan, huh?

419
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:39,600
Why didn't you tell me this?

420
00:23:51,360 --> 00:23:52,920
Anyone but him?

421
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,380
And why now?

422
00:23:55,860 --> 00:24:00,000
Lord Orochi, sir, we await your order.

423
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:02,299
What would you have us do with him?

424
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,737
Do you really need to ask?

425
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,140
The man must die!

426
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:11,740
Make an example of him
with a public execution!

427
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:14,380
Put it on lightstraws everywhere!

428
00:24:14,740 --> 00:24:16,620
Make certain that all can see!

429
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,560
It's already taken care of.

430
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,860
Don't you worry.

431
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:22,370
Kyoshiro!

432
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:27,180
As you know, today is the day that
Komorosaki's public funeral will be held.

433
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:29,437
With so many people in attendance,

434
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:32,520
we expect that the event
might become a bit unruly.

435
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:35,020
I took it upon myself to prepare.

436
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:38,560
Yes, yes! Splendid!

437
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,720
What is your order, sir?

438
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:50,757
all right i have an idea yes
have him personally accompany

439
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:55,320
kumasaki to the grave that wretched
little bastard will die today

440
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:04,617
it's a two-for-one funeral some
of the brightest stars of the city

441
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:11,437
buried together what a wicked twist
of fate excellent thinking my lord now

442
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:14,557
bring me my ride i intend to witness

443
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:21,517
the entire tragedy go down that's not

444
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:27,300
funny you're in the booze early again
aren't you kaido stop joking around

445
00:25:30,280 --> 00:25:35,097
sorry it's true it's no
fair it can't be go check

446
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:38,520
your freaking light scroll
if you don't believe me.

447
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:42,340
It killed me!

448
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,030
Ah!

449
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:46,790
Komurasaki!

450
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:51,000
It's over.

451
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:52,857
We couldn't hide it.

452
00:25:52,940 --> 00:25:54,757
He knows about the Oiran's death.

453
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:56,500
This is going to suck.

454
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,417
Expect him to be moody for weeks.

455
00:25:58,500 --> 00:25:59,640
That's no good.

456
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,240
Can we do something?

457
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:03,210
Hey!

458
00:26:03,860 --> 00:26:05,297
Come on, Balloon!

459
00:26:05,380 --> 00:26:08,180
Dude, why is taking so long?

460
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:10,400
Shut up!

461
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:12,900
There's been a change of plans now.

462
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:14,370
Huh?

463
00:26:14,453 --> 00:26:16,100
Not if I say so!

464
00:26:16,380 --> 00:26:18,220
Let's get going already!

465
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:20,580
We don't have all day!

466
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:22,010
Oh?

467
00:26:22,093 --> 00:26:25,717
What the hell happened to you
two between last night and today?

468
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,506
This is what I'm always like.

469
00:26:27,740 --> 00:26:29,093
What you talking about?

470
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:31,617
Oh, are you sure?

471
00:26:31,700 --> 00:26:35,117
Hey, you think it's a bad time to
tell him all his soup went missing?

472
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:38,117
Overnight too are you dumb who knows what

473
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:41,300
he'll do if he's hit with
more bad news i agree?

474
00:26:42,700 --> 00:26:47,317
Kind of wondering how that much food
just uh walked away you did hear

475
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:52,357
me yes i advised Sir Luffy not to
gorge himself devouring the entire

476
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:56,237
pot was irresponsible of him given
his Circumstance how does this

477
00:26:56,320 --> 00:27:01,160
idiot keep surviving what is his
secret let's start the sumo match!

478
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:07,760
I ain't got time to deal
with your nonsense today.

479
00:27:07,980 --> 00:27:10,940
I have something to tend to. Hey, you.

480
00:27:11,140 --> 00:27:13,440
Show me the flower capital right now.

481
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:15,460
Get the light scroll snail.

482
00:27:18,740 --> 00:27:19,940
It's prepared.

483
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,280
Ready for signal.

484
00:27:24,260 --> 00:27:26,460
Let's see what's going on over there.

485
00:27:27,080 --> 00:27:29,380
A video transponder snail.

486
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:31,130
Oh, no.

487
00:27:33,380 --> 00:27:34,560
Oh, I see.

488
00:27:34,820 --> 00:27:37,140
That must be the flower capital.

489
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:49,060
They dared to steal our food and weapons.

490
00:27:49,260 --> 00:27:53,980
Show the Otamayama Thieves Brigade
what happens to those who cross us.

491
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:55,960
I'm tired of going in circles.

492
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:04,260
I'll shut your lying mouth with
my trick mechanism so hard!

493
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:12,560
Won't be long before the Atamayama
Thieves Brigade collapses.

494
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:21,660
The fire's spreading too fast!

495
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:24,280
We can't put it out. It's massive.

496
00:28:26,540 --> 00:28:28,540
Damn, Hold 'em screwed us over!

497
00:28:29,260 --> 00:28:31,060
They're turned to Bekori Town!

498
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:32,400
Are you sure, sir?

499
00:28:32,900 --> 00:28:35,477
Will Kaido's men come
after us if we go there?

500
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:37,540
What makes you think I care?

501
00:28:38,140 --> 00:28:39,200
So what?

502
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:41,680
I'll kick all their asses!

503
00:28:46,340 --> 00:28:47,400
That's a shame.

504
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:51,040
In that case, Ashura Doji
has my deepest sympathy.

505
00:28:51,700 --> 00:28:52,530
Indeed.

506
00:28:52,613 --> 00:28:54,635
And yet this was for the greater good.

507
00:28:55,000 --> 00:29:00,977
Despite its dire cost let's travel
to Bakada town I know not what

508
00:29:01,060 --> 00:29:04,857
direction to take Now that our
initial plans have been thwarted we

509
00:29:04,940 --> 00:29:08,697
shall focus on one task ensuring
that Ashita goes to battle with our

510
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:14,060
enemy Otherwise I fear our struggle
may be lost before it even begins

511
00:29:20,340 --> 00:29:21,170
I'm back

512
00:29:29,820 --> 00:29:32,340
Excuse me, who the heck is that?

513
00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:35,079
What in the world is going on here?

514
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:38,620
Oh, hey, Brooke What's up with you?

515
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,140
Why are you here?

516
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:46,680
Oh, Zoro If I had ice, they would be
bugging out at the sight I'm seeing.

517
00:29:46,900 --> 00:29:50,547
Although I suppose I could
literally drop my jaw to the floor.

518
00:29:51,840 --> 00:29:53,237
Apologies for the intrusion.

519
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:54,732
I'll see myself out now.

520
00:29:55,220 --> 00:29:57,377
Wait, hey, it's not what it looks like.

521
00:29:57,460 --> 00:29:59,140
Get back here. Huh?

522
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:00,740
Don't mind if I do.

523
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,180
My mistake, then.

524
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:05,930
Whoa.

525
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:06,843
What beauty.

526
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:11,077
Pardon me for being so bold, but may
I have a look at your panties, please?

527
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:11,990
Huh?

528
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:23,660
It's fine he's a friend

529
00:30:26,660 --> 00:30:30,700
Prepare for me a fine feast
or else I shall curse you!

530
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:33,380
I'm scared

531
00:30:35,220 --> 00:30:37,817
Kin'emon instructed me to
stay here and scare off

532
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:40,617
people with that whole
haunted house bed I see.

533
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:41,530
How funny.

534
00:30:41,613 --> 00:30:44,840
I wondered why so many people
left offerings outside.

535
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:49,377
Wow, it's incredible to think that you
were the younger sister of Momonosuke.

536
00:30:49,460 --> 00:30:52,400
Beautiful like the Oiran,
a sight for sore eyes.

537
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:53,900
If I had a bear!

538
00:30:54,540 --> 00:30:57,040
Because she is an Oiran, silly!

539
00:30:57,360 --> 00:30:59,737
How did you settle down
with someone like her?

540
00:30:59,820 --> 00:31:01,260
I'm quite envious, Oro.

541
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:04,040
We were only sleeping, you dumbass.

542
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:05,920
Please tell him. Apologies.

543
00:31:06,260 --> 00:31:09,613
It was freezing and body heat
is a good source of warmth.

544
00:31:10,180 --> 00:31:11,437
However, you're lucky.

545
00:31:11,520 --> 00:31:14,637
Men are usually besotted by the
thought of sleeping next to me.

546
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:16,073
You should be thankful.

547
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:18,520
So be honest, you loved it, right?

548
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:21,440
Damn, you are pretty forward, lady. Yes.

549
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:26,297
Anyway, I hope that the rest of
our crew isn't too far behind us.

550
00:31:26,380 --> 00:31:28,657
The women set out to use
the bathhouse yesterday,

551
00:31:28,740 --> 00:31:32,564
but when I tried to find them, it
was no use, as you might guess.

552
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:37,100
Also, the flower capital is in a
state of chaos, if you didn't know.

553
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:39,877
People are pouring into
the city by the masses.

554
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:43,313
It's the funeral of Wano's
most beautiful woman, you see.

555
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:48,917
And they captured some thief who
steals money and gives to the poor.

556
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:52,317
Ushimitsu Koza is his name, and
he seems as if he was a big deal.

557
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:53,897
Where did you hear that news?

558
00:31:53,980 --> 00:31:56,700
It can't be. No, it's all true. Here.

559
00:31:57,760 --> 00:31:59,407
Read about it in this flyer.

560
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:01,974
He'll be executed in the capital today.

561
00:32:02,140 --> 00:32:04,777
His real identity has been
a mystery until recently.

562
00:32:04,860 --> 00:32:07,700
Sounds like he was quite
beloved in Ebisu Town.

563
00:32:08,040 --> 00:32:10,380
Did you say Ebisu Town? Oh, yeah.

564
00:32:10,660 --> 00:32:11,937
And there's more written.

565
00:32:12,020 --> 00:32:15,937
If I remember, he goes by the
name something Yasuie, I think.

566
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:16,877
Chono Yasuie?

567
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:17,901
That's the name?

568
00:32:18,020 --> 00:32:18,902
How'd you know?

569
00:32:21,980 --> 00:32:22,810
Chaka.

570
00:32:33,480 --> 00:32:35,060
Hey, what's with her?

571
00:32:35,220 --> 00:32:36,220
Come back, Chaka!

572
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:41,052
Thank you for saving our lives yesterday.

573
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:43,358
We shall never forget your kindness.

574
00:32:43,540 --> 00:32:44,680
Don't be stupid!

575
00:32:44,980 --> 00:32:46,577
You couldn't even protect her by yourself!

576
00:32:46,660 --> 00:32:47,490
I'm going!

577
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:50,997
Where are you guys all running to?

578
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:52,160
I just got here!

579
00:32:52,460 --> 00:32:55,520
Wait up! Everyone! Hey!

580
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:10,660
Get up.

581
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:11,780
Time to go.

582
00:33:12,460 --> 00:33:13,290
Greetings.

583
00:33:13,373 --> 00:33:14,800
You come to escort me.

584
00:33:15,020 --> 00:33:17,079
That is mighty kind of you fellows.

585
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:31,750
What?

586
00:33:31,833 --> 00:33:32,700
It can't be.

587
00:33:33,060 --> 00:33:34,060
He was caught?

588
00:33:41,620 --> 00:33:43,796
Where do you think you're going, kid?

589
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:47,038
There's people who want you
dead out there, remember?

590
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:49,537
Stop it! Let go!

591
00:33:49,620 --> 00:33:51,600
He needs my help! Calm down!

592
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:53,057
We've got to get a grip!

593
00:33:53,140 --> 00:33:54,040
Let me go!

594
00:33:55,900 --> 00:33:58,260
What has gotten into her? Taco!

595
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,740
They're going to kill him!

596
00:34:02,280 --> 00:34:03,840
Please let me go!

597
00:34:04,100 --> 00:34:05,960
I have to help him somehow!

598
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:08,960
My daddy will die if I don't go!

599
00:34:13,700 --> 00:34:14,530
Taco...

600
00:34:14,613 --> 00:34:15,829
What the hell did you say?

601
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:23,840
What fine weather today.

602
00:34:24,180 --> 00:34:27,100
Such a pleasant time to
be in the flower capital.
